{
  "_note": "The CO2 malus is charged on the first French registration, an import from another member state included, and the scale is the one of the year the car was FIRST registered anywhere — not the year it reaches France (arts. L.421-59, L.421-62 to L.421-64). A car first registered before 1 January 2015 owes nothing at all (L.421-60). WLTP scales apply from 2020, the NEDC ones to European type approvals before that, and a car with no European approval falls to a scale on fiscal horsepower we cannot read, since we do not know its CV. The weight malus is a separate tax needing a kerb mass we do not have; L.421-74 caps the two together at the top of the CO2 scale.",
